+# Direct joint legal-set construction — 9 October 2026
+
+## Question and prospective mechanism
+
+Can a direct constrained choice of legal Prefix/Generate destinations form a
+protected descending offer where #2117 residual feedback offered none? The
+[saved diagnosis](../discrete-feedback-attribution-2026-10-09/README.md) authenticated
+28 distinct failures, with 338/380 violated-row union and no universal veto.
+This changes proposal formation, not gradients, Source authority, memory access,
+serving operators, native acceptance or model capacity.
+
+[Prospective M2 claim](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/2030#issuecomment-6092186833).
+**Implementation and execution pending. No model result or promotion.** Accepted
+Source48/Generate64 remains 8/512 complete development replies; separate conditional
+9/15 is not this original 5/15 epoch and cannot be combined with it.
+
+All 1920 original master coordinates and all 15 legal destinations remain available.
+For original code q0=round_ties_away(4m), the noop retains m's original f32 bits;
+each other q in[-7,7] uses q/4. For noncanonical m, use integer q and binary l,r:
+
+```text
+l + r <= 1
+q >= q0 + r - (q0 + 7) l
+q <= q0 - l + (7 - q0) r
+delta = (q - q0)/4 + (l + r)(q0/4 - m)
+```
+
+The three branches cover exactly noop/lower/upper legal codes, including endpoint
+codes. Canonical masters need only q; all decoded noops still retain original bits,
+including negative zero. No answer, token, named guard or named coordinate has an
+exception. Minimize original g·delta subject to all 380 unitJ·delta>=0.
+
+**This zero-margin construction target is stricter than the existing numerical
+admission domain** unitJ·delta>=-1e-10||delta||. It is an explicit inner target, not
+a replacement or weakening of the gate. An unsuccessful search does not cover
+all legal destinations admitted only by that norm tolerance.
+
+Backend: pinned [microlp 0.6.0](https://docs.rs/microlp/0.6.0/microlp/), pure Rust,
+used offline in the training tool only. Use its integer branch-and-bound with a
+fixed 4096-node bound (root relaxation excluded by backend), zero/noop warm start,
+no time cutoff, and at most one returned incumbent. No new hand-written numerical
+optimizer, random seed sweep, radius tuning or residual-feedback schedule.
+The backend warns that difficult problems may lose precision or cycle. Its
+floating-point optimal/infeasible statuses are observations, not mathematical
+certificates. A bounded search returning only noop is not strict descent.
+
+Reconstruct complete legal destination bits from unambiguous integer decisions,
+recompute actual f64 delta, g·delta and all 380 unit-J residuals in the existing
+order, and apply the unchanged strict descent and relative-tolerance screen. Recomputed
+zero-margin satisfaction is a separate diagnostic: small solver-numerical negatives
+may pass the existing relative tolerance, which remains the admission authority.
+Only then may the existing coherent 391-row native transaction score the proposal.
+Keep strict combined/episode CE descent, all 17 reference roles, all 380 original
+winners, exact selected restage and atomic commit, independent saved reload, and
+all 15 conditional positions before positive-only actual-nine qualification.
+
+## Fixed evidence and outcomes
+
+Import the existing authenticated #2101 saved objective and protected derivatives
+through the existing strict importer, using #2117's verified input restoration.
+No new backward or training-graph calls. Same original development input 245
+conditional episode including EOS, 17 reference roles, 380 original guards and 391
+unique native row union; no held-out data. Do not change the model's windows,
+Source eligibility, parameters outside Prefix/Generate unary, or canonical data.
+
+- A screened legal offer and native success advance export/reload/actual-nine.
+- A screened offer with native veto distinguishes finite native behavior from the
+  first-order surrogate; it does not establish model incapacity.
+- No descending offer is unresolved bounded search under the zero-margin target,
+  not a global infeasibility result or permission to enlarge the bound afterward.
+- Numerical/setup failures remain execution evidence, not model-quality negatives.
+
+## Checks and resources
+
+Before actual execution: exact legal-domain fixtures including fractional/noop/
+signed-zero/endpoints, small constrained problems, joint repair where
+single moves fail, no-descending/no-incumbent distinctions, numerical decoding and
+unchanged native stage/rollback fixtures; source review and exact-head build.
+Use scoped tests, claim wording, geometry connection checks and regenerated figures.
+
+Complete projection: 90 minutes, two CPU threads, 6 GiB constructor process RAM (existing 3.56 GiB
+transaction projection plus 2 GiB solver reserve), 3 GiB compile estimate, 6 GiB transient disk,
+512 MiB reports; initially 38 GiB free versus 30 GiB + 128 MiB floor. Same-class local
+allowance was extended 90 minutes before implementation to 1,463,400,028 ms, preserving
+cumulative 1,456,254,279 ms and continuing charges since 01:24:55.251810Z. No GPU, pod,
+paid compute, Python model or new serving dependency. A healthy run is not cancelled
+at a self-estimated wall time; the solver's fixed node bound defines this mechanism.
+
+**Next:** Finish and review the constructor, run the single declared saved-credit
+construction and preserve its native disposition before choosing any successor.
